<!-- ===================== THE THEFT — NAMED PLAINLY ======================= -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame caution">
    <p class="kicker">Limb VIII · Required Reading</p>
    <h2>The Theft of the Staves</h2>
    <p>You cannot study this alphabet honestly and walk past this, so we will not.</p>
    <p>Guido von List, blind after a cataract operation in 1902, claimed to have received an
    eighteen-rune "Armanen" futhark — a set that never existed, built to fit the eighteen charms of the
    <em>Hávamál</em> and an Austrian-German racial mysticism. ◆ Myth, and a deliberate one. Through the
    Ariosophists it passed to Karl Maria Wiligut and from there into the SS, where Sowilo was doubled into
    the Schutzstaffel insignia, Algiz became the <em>Lebensrune</em> on birth announcements and gravestones,
    Tiwaz marked Hitler Youth leadership courses, and Odal was stitched onto a division that murdered
    civilians.</p>
    <p>None of this made the regime occult, and we are careful about that claim: the Nazi state was an
    industrial atrocity run by a bureaucracy, and its leadership was largely contemptuous of the mystics it
    tolerated. The runes were not a source of its power. They were <strong>stolen decoration</strong> —
    antiquity borrowed to make a new and murderous movement look like an inheritance rather than an
    invention. That is the only accurate reading, and it is worse than the occult one, not better.</p>
    <p>The order's position: the Elder Futhark belongs to the people who cut it into combs and spear-shafts
    seventeen centuries ago, and not to its thieves. Learn which shapes still carry that freight in public —
    Algiz, Odal, the doubled Sowilo — know why, and do not be naive about who you are standing next to when
    you wear one. Reclamation is possible; it is done by knowing the history out loud, never by pretending
    there isn't one.</p>
    <p class="muted small">See also: <a href="/ask-ed/">the Black Tribunal material</a>, on enforced
    integration with the choices of previous beings — nothing disowned, nothing romanticised.</p>
  </div>
</section>

