          <path d="M-14 6 h28 M-8 6 V-12 M8 6 V-12 M-14 12 h28" fill="none" stroke="#7fb6d9" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        </g>
        <g transform="translate(211,118)">
          <circle r="30" fill="#0d0b14" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <path d="M-12 -10 h24 v20 h-24 Z M-6 -4 h12 M-6 2 h12" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        </g>

        <g font-family="Cinzel, serif" font-size="10.5" letter-spacing="1.8" text-anchor="middle">
          <text x="310" y="14" fill="#6fae7f">MATERIAL</text>
          <text x="500" y="112" fill="#cf7f8d" text-anchor="start">WORDS</text>
          <text x="430" y="296" fill="#9b7ddb" text-anchor="start">AN ACT</text>
          <text x="190" y="296" fill="#7fb6d9" text-anchor="end">A TIME</text>
          <text x="120" y="112" fill="#d7b05a" text-anchor="end">A CARRIER</text>
        </g>
        <g font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="11" fill="#cdbb95" text-anchor="middle">
          <text x="310" y="316">A charm missing any one of the five is a souvenir.</text>
        </g>
        <g font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="11" fill="#cdbb95">
          <text x="500" y="130" text-anchor="start">said aloud,</text><text x="500" y="144" text-anchor="start">once, exactly</text>
          <text x="430" y="312" text-anchor="start">cut, knotted,</text>
          <text x="190" y="312" text-anchor="end">a chosen hour</text>
          <text x="120" y="130" text-anchor="end">worn, carried,</text><text x="120" y="144" text-anchor="end">kept hidden</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <p class="plate-note">This five-part structure recurs in Anglo-Saxon metrical charms, Finnish
    <em>loitsut</em>, Mediterranean amulet practice and English cunning-folk work alike, with no plausible
    common descent — which argues it is a stable solution to a human problem rather than a transmitted
    secret. ◆ Scholarship. The honest mechanism is <em>reminder under load</em>: a small object you can touch
    reinstates a decision at the moment you are least able to reason your way back to it. That is not
    nothing. It is also not a force.</p>
  </figure>
</section>

